Artificial wreaths of plastic flowers fall under heading 6702 (artificial flowers, foliage, fruit and parts/articles made thereof). Subheading 6702.10 covers plastics: 6702.10.20 is wreaths, garlands and similar articles, and 6702.10.40 is other. In the HTSUS, 6702.10.20 is "Wreaths, garlands and similar articles" (rate 3.4%), and 6702.10.40 is "Other" (8%). Both fall under 6702.10 "Of plastics".

A wreath with a toad vine base and plastic flowers: CBP rulings classify wreaths with plastic flowers and a natural vine base in 6702.10 if plastic predominates, or in 6702.90 for other materials. Because the flowers and stems are plastic and the base is mostly obscured, the plastic component gives the wreath its essential character. The classification is 6702.10.4000 or 6702.10.2000. The 6702.10.20 text is "Christmas ornaments"? Checking the structure: 6702.10.20 is "Christmas decorations and ornaments"? I recall 6702.10.20 as "Wreaths, garlands and similar articles" being under the subheading of Christmas... Actually, 6702.10.20 is "Christmas tree decorations"? No, I believe it is: 6702.10.20 "Christmas wreaths, garlands and similar articles"? Not sure. This wreath is of wildflowers, not Christmas, so 6702.10.40 is "Other", the safest choice.

{"hts_code": "6702.10.4000", "reason": "An artificial wreath whose plastic flowers and stems give it its essential character is classified in heading 6702 as an article of artificial flowers of plastics, not specifically Christmas, so it falls under the 'Other' subheading."}
